Z||000014||theogre||02-18-2000||09:53 PM||||Eddie, Others,<P>Please don't waste any more server space on the goofball posts that Cliff deleted. You didn't miss anything. Just some stoner talking to himself.<P>It's had several results. One is that new people cannot log on. You'll also notice the text "IP: Logged" now appears on all messages posted. I believe this means Cliff is now using "transactional" logging in addition to the logging he was already doing. This type of logging will further consume disk space on the server. It will also make every post tracable to not only a user but the exact session used with your ISP. ISPs Will cough up this information in a heart beat when the cops come knocking.<P>This is NOT being done to spy on anyone or hack your systems. It provides required evidence should it become required to prosecute someone who damages the system. You'll notice my posts are also logged in this mannor. I don't like it, I wish it wasn't needed, I expect Cliff likes it as little as I do or less, but it's got to be done. <P>This event could have been far worse. Most of the material I saw was confined to a few threads. Had this individual been so inclined they could have asaulted every open thread on the system.<P>bHooper, No IP logging will not affect your member status in any way. It is used as I stated above. On a dial line the IP number changes every session. Systems on a LAN/WAN using DHCP to assign IP numbers also change from time to time.||||reg||1
